        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>FBbt:00007325</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>While insect epidermis is generally columnar/cuboidal, there are certainly well studied cases where it is not (e.g.- Rhodnius prolixus when starved). So it would be safer to add this as a differentium for particular species where this is known. -DSJ.</rdfs:comment>
