            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A progenitor cell committed to the basophil lineage. This cell lacks hematopoietic lineage markers (lin-negative) and is CD34-positive, T1/ST2-low, CD117-negative, and FceRIa-high. This cell also expresses Gata-1, Gata-2 and C/EBPa.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>BaP</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>CFU-Bas</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>basophilic stem cell</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>colony forming unit basophil</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:comment>BaP are also CD13-low and integrin beta-7-low. They are lin-negative (CD2, CD3e, CD4, CD5, CD8, CD11b, CD14, CD19, CD20, ly6g, ly76, and NCAM-1). They also lack expression of mast cell protease 1 (MCP-1) and microphthalmia-associated transcription factor (mitf).</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>basophil progenitor cell</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
