        <obo:IAO_0000115>A neuron with soma location in the central nervous system that project its axon to the contralateral side of a central nervous system. This neuron can have its soma in the spinal cord, in the hemisphere of the brain, in the retina or in the ventral nerve cord of invertebrates.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:comment>Historically, commissural neurons, particularly in the spinal cord, have been used as a model to understand axon guidance during development.</rdfs:comment>
