        <obo:IAO_0000115>A Be cell that facilitates development of T-helper 1 (Th1) phenotype in CD4-positive T cells, and secretes high levels of interleukin-2, tumor necrosis factor-alpha and interferon-gamma.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>B effector 1 cell</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>B effector cell type 1</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:comment>Be1 cells are also reportedly capable of secreting IL-6, IL-10, and IL-12. They are also reportedly CD11b-negative and B220-positive.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Be1 Cell</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
