    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CL_0002069">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CL_0000609"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Mostly cylindrical, resemble Type 1 in their contents and the presence of a kinocilium and stereocilium apically; much greater variation in size, some almost span the entire thickness of the sensory epithelium, while others are smaller than Type 1; receive multiple efferent nerve boutons around their bases as well as afferent endings, which are small expansions rather than chalices.</obo:IAO_0000115>
