        <owl:annotatedTarget>The prototypic neuron projects to downstream basal ganglia nuclei, including the subthalamic nucleus (STN), internal globus pallidus, and substantia nigra pars reticulata (SNr), with some neurons also emitting ascending collaterals that modestly innervate the striatum (Mallet et al., 2012, Abdi et al., 2015). It exhibits longer local axon collaterals with more boutons compared to arkypallidal neurons, supporting extensive local interconnectivity within the GPe (Mallet et al., 2012). The prototypic neuron plays a fundamental role in the indirect pathway of the basal ganglia, coordinating activity across basal ganglia nuclei through its widespread projections (Mallet et al., 2012, Courtney et al., 2023). Decreases in firing during movement are consistent with disinhibiting the STN and output nuclei, thereby facilitating the expression of desired motor patterns (Dodson et al., 2015, Courtney et al., 2023).</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:22726837</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
