            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A dentate gyrus neuron with soma in the polymorphic layer (Scharfman &amp; Myers, 2012), capable of glutamate secretion as a neurotransmitter (Scharfman &amp; Bernstein, 2015). Distinguished by a large multipolar soma, thorny excrescences on proximal dendrites, and commissural/associational axon projections terminating in the inner molecular layer of the dentate gyrus (Scharfman &amp; Myers, 2012). In rodents, serves as a major excitatory neuron of the dentate hilus providing feedback excitation to granule cells (Sun et al., 2017).</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000233 rdf:resource="https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/3648"/>
        <terms:contributor rdf:resource="https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5507-2103"/>
        <terms:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2026-05-21T10:51:40Z</terms:date>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>dentate hilar mossy cell</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>mossy cell</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <rdfs:label>hilar mossy cell</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    <owl:Axiom>
