        <owl:annotatedTarget>A dentate gyrus neuron with soma in the polymorphic layer (Scharfman &amp; Myers, 2012), capable of glutamate secretion as a neurotransmitter (Scharfman &amp; Bernstein, 2015). Distinguished by a large multipolar soma, thorny excrescences on proximal dendrites, and commissural/associational axon projections terminating in the inner molecular layer of the dentate gyrus (Scharfman &amp; Myers, 2012). In rodents, serves as a major excitatory neuron of the dentate hilus providing feedback excitation to granule cells (Sun et al., 2017).</owl:annotatedTarget>
