        <owl:annotatedTarget>The extratelencephalic-projecting glutamatergic cortical neuron is a vital cell subtype found within the cerebral cortex. Belonging to the broader class of glutamatergic neurons, this neuron type is characterized by its output connections that stretch outside the telencephalon, a region encompassing the cerebrum in the brain. This classification is notable for the release of glutamate, an excitatory neurotransmitter, which plays a pivotal role in neural communication, memory formation, learning, and regulation of various neurodevelopmental and neuropathological processes.
