        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CL_4030059"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>Hystorically, the L2/3 intratelencephalic projectic glutametergic neuron was known to have its soma in cortical layer 2/3. MERFISH data showed that this intratelencephalic-projecting glutametergic neuron can have its soma in layer 2/3, 4B, 4C. The position of the soma in layer 4b and 4C is less frequent for this neuronal type in comparison to cortical layer 2/3.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:37824655</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CL_4030059"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>The marker set ONECUT2, COL5A2 can identify the Human cell type L2/3 intratelencephalic projecting glutamatergic neuron in the neocortex with a confidence of 0.670149932 (NS-Forest FBeta value).</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.11165918</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


