                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLM_1001259"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>An ON bipolar cell type with dendrites selectively contacting S-cones.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:RO_0002175 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCBITaxon_9606"/>
        <terms:contributor rdf:resource="https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6677-8489"/>
        <terms:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2023-04-04T09:48:15Z</terms:date>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>BB cell</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/cl#added_by_HRA"/>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/cl#cellxgene_subset"/>
        <rdfs:comment>The axons of a blue cone bipolar cell terminate close to the ganglion cell layer, where they transfer the S-cone ON signal to small bistratified ganglion cells. Other targets of a blue cone bipolar cell include amacrine cells and possibly large bistratified ganglion cells.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:comment>The marker set SORCS3, TAFA1 can identify the Human cell type http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CL_4033019 in the retina with a confidence of 0.709302326 (NS-Forest FBeta value).</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:comment>The marker set TAFA1, ENSG00000250971 can identify the Human cell type http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CL_4033019 in the retina with a confidence of 0.797269292 (NS-Forest FBeta value).</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>ON-blue cone bipolar cell</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:seeAlso rdf:resource="https://celltype.info/project/544/dataset/1157"/>
    </owl:Class>
