        <obo:IAO_0000115>A central nervous system macrophage that is part of a choroid plexus, a meninx and a perivascular space. A border associated macrophage interacts with various components of the CNS vasculature and meninges, it participates in immune surveillance and in the regulation of the blood brain barrier.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <terms:contributor rdf:resource="https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0098-8958"/>
        <terms:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2024-03-26T16:39:56Z</terms:date>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>BAM</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>CAM</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>CNS-associated macrophage</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:comment>In humans, a border associate macrophage expresses CD45 and CD11B. This cell is also known to have the following molecular signature: CD206, CD38, LYVE1, CD163, CD169.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">border associated macrophage</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
