        <owl:annotatedTarget>The S2 fibroblast population has been identified as a subset of intestinal fibroblasts located near the epithelial lining. This population is divided into two subtypes: S2a and S2b. S2a is involved in epithelial differentiation, while S2b, located at the top of the crypt, regulates intestinal stem cell proliferation, niche formation, and wound healing.</owl:annotatedTarget>
