            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0002162"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCBITaxon_9606"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000028>L4 IT (Homo sapiens)</obo:IAO_0000028>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A transcriptomically distinct intratelencephalic-projecting glutamatergic neuron with a soma found in cortical layer 3-4. This neuron type can have a pyramidal, star-pyramidal or spiny stellate morphology and projects its output to L2/3 and L5A/B. The standard transcriptomic reference data for this cell type can be found on the CellxGene census under the collection: &apos;Transcriptomic cytoarchitecture reveals principles of human neocortex organization&apos;, dataset: &apos;Supercluster: IT-projecting excitatory neurons&apos;, Author Categories: &apos;CrossArea_subclass&apos;, L4 IT.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:RO_0002175 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCBITaxon_9606"/>
        <terms:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2025-09-10T10:05:26Z</terms:date>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>L4 IT (Homo sapiens)</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/cl#cellxgene_subset"/>
        <rdfs:comment>The marker set RORB, ST8SIA4 can identify the Human cell type L4 intratelencephalic projecting glutamatergic neuron in the neocortex with a confidence of 0.720108696 (NS-Forest FBeta value).</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>L4 intratelencephalic projecting glutamatergic neuron (Homo sapiens)</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
